{%- comment -%}
  Fetch user + CRM company + CRM default address in one query so we can
  pre-fill the location record with the user's existing company details
  on first visit. Falls back gracefully when any of these relations
  are missing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- graphql user = 'modules/locator/account/get_my_user_with_crm' | dig: 'current_user' -%}
{%- assign crm_contact = user.crm_contact | first -%}
{%- assign crm_company = crm_contact.crm_company -%}
{%- assign crm_address = crm_company.crm_address -%}
{%- graphql location_result = 'modules/locator/locations/get_my_location', user_uuid: user.external_id | dig: 'relation','results' | first -%}
{%- assign location = location_result | dig: 'location' -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Orphan cleanup. The admin can delete a location record from the front-end
  admin UI without removing the related location_custom_field row(s), which
  leaves the user with one or more join rows whose location_uuid no longer
  resolves (location_result.location is null). Sample shape we're handling:
    { "location_uuid": "a041404a-…", "location": null }

  When detected, wipe ALL the user's location_custom_field rows (there may be
  more than one, all orphaned), then reset location_result so the bootstrap
  block below runs and creates a fresh, valid pair.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if location_result.location_uuid != blank and location_result.location == blank -%}
  {%- graphql cleanup_result = 'modules/locator/locations/delete_my_location_custom_fields', user_uuid: user.external_id -%}
  {%- assign location_result = nil -%}
  {%- assign location = nil -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  First-visit bootstrap. If the user has no location_custom_field row yet, the
  join returns no results and `location` is blank. Without this, the listing
  forms would submit in CREATE mode but the `location_custom_field` join row
  would never be created, so on the next page load `get_my_location` would
  still return nil and the user's save would appear to have vanished.

  Create both rows up-front:
    - location record with status: 'disabled' (so the listing stays hidden
      until the user toggles visibility on) and a fresh uuid
    - location_custom_field join row linking user_uuid <-> location_uuid

  Then re-fetch so the rest of the page renders in UPDATE mode just like the
  returning-user path.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if location_result.location_uuid == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Seed `location_name` from the user's CRM company. Required by the
    location schema, so we fall back through:
      1. crm_company.company_name (preferred — real business name)
      2. crm_company.uuid          (still unique, less friendly)
      3. user.external_id          (last-resort guarantee of non-blank)
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign initial_location_name = crm_company.company_name | default: crm_company.uuid | default: user.external_id -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Create Location and Location Custom Field user_uuid
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- parse_json params -%}
  {
    "status": "disabled",
    "location_name": "{{ initial_location_name }}",
    "email": "{{ crm_company.email_1 }}",
    "phone_number": "{{ crm_company.mobile_phone_number }}",
    "phone_country_code": "{{ crm_company.mobile_phone_country_code }}",
    "website": "{{ crm_company.website }}",
    "address_1": "{{ crm_address.address_1 }}",
    "address_2": "{{ crm_address.address_2 }}",
    "address_3": "{{ crm_address.address_3 }}",
    "city": "{{ crm_address.city }}",
    "county": "{{ crm_address.county }}",
    "district": "{{ crm_address.district }}",
    "suburb": "{{ crm_address.suburb }}",
    "state": "{{ crm_address.state }}",
    "country": "{{ crm_address.country }}",
    "country_code": "{{ crm_address.country_code }}",
    "postcode": "{{ crm_address.postcode }}",
    "latitude": "{{ crm_address.latitude }}",
    "longitude": "{{ crm_address.longitude }}",
    "facebook_link": "{{ crm_company.facebook_link }}",
    "twitter_link": "{{ crm_company.twitter_link }}",
    "youtube_link": "{{ crm_company.youtube_link }}",
    "linkedin_link": "{{ crm_company.linkedin_link }}",
    "instagram_link": "{{ crm_company.instagram_link }}",
    "snapchat_link": "{{ crm_company.snapchat_link }}",
    "social_1_link": "{{ crm_company.social_1_link }}",
    "social_2_link": "{{ crm_company.social_2_link }}",
    "custom_field.user_uuid": "{{ user.external_id }}"
  }
  {%- endparse_json -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The controller writes BOTH the location row AND the location_custom_field
    join row in one call — the `custom_field.user_uuid` entry above is what
    triggers the join-row insert (location_uuid is auto-added, user_uuid comes
    from this param). So we don't call create_location_custom_field separately.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% function created_location = "locator/controller/locations/create", params: params %}

  {%- graphql location_result = 'modules/locator/locations/get_my_location', user_uuid: user.external_id | dig: 'relation','results' | first -%}
  {%- assign location = location_result | dig: 'location' -%}
{%- endif -%}


{%- graphql categories_result = 'modules/locator/categories/get_categories' -%}
{%- assign categories = categories_result | dig: 'items','results' -%}

<div class="my-locator-listing">
  <div class="locator-listing__head">
    <div class="locator-listing__head-row">
      <div class="locator-listing__head-text">
        <h1 class="heading-1-xsmall">My locator listing</h1>
        <p>Update your public profile and control whether you appear on the partner locator.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-listing__actions">
        {%- comment -%}
          "Preview my listing" — visible only when the listing is enabled.
          Requires a slug; on a brand-new user the slug is generated async
          after the first profile save, so we skip the link entirely when
          slug is blank to avoid a broken /find-a-partner/ URL. JS keeps
          the .hide state in sync with the toggle below.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if location.slug != blank -%}
          <a href="/find-a-partner/{{ location.slug }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
             id="locator-preview-link"
             class="locator-listing__preview-link{% unless location.status == 'enabled' %} hide{% endunless %}">
            <ins-button label="Preview my listing" icon-right="icon-arrow-up-right" outlined color="primary"></ins-button>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="locator-listing__visibility">
          <span class="form-label" id="locator-visibility-label">Public Visibility:</span>
          <ins-toggle-switch
            id="locator-visibility"
            name="visibility"
            role="switch"
            aria-labelledby="locator-visibility-label"
            {% if location.status == 'enabled' %}checked{% endif %}
          ></ins-toggle-switch>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="spacer x-large"></div>

  <div id="locator-visibility-banner" role="status" aria-live="polite"{% if location.status == 'enabled' %} class="hide"{% endif %}>
    <div class="locator-listing__visibility-banner">
      <i class="icon-info" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span>Your listing is hidden. Changes will be saved but won't appear on the partner directory until you turn visibility on.</span>      
    </div>
    <div class="spacer x-large"></div>
  </div>

  {%- liquid
    assign active_tab = 'profile'
    if context.flash
      assign flash_msg = context.flash.notice | default: context.flash.alert
      if flash_msg contains 'Listing-Location'
        assign active_tab = 'location'
      elsif flash_msg contains 'Listing-Social'
        assign active_tab = 'social'
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  <ins-tab>
    <ins-tab-item label="Profile" {% if active_tab == 'profile' %}active{% endif %}>
      {%- include_form 'modules/locator/listing_profile', id: location.id, data: location -%}
    </ins-tab-item>
    <ins-tab-item label="Location" {% if active_tab == 'location' %}active{% endif %}>
      {%- include_form 'modules/locator/listing_location', id: location.id, data: location -%}
    </ins-tab-item>
    <ins-tab-item label="Social links" {% if active_tab == 'social' %}active{% endif %}>
      {%- include_form 'modules/locator/listing_social', id: location.id, data: location -%}
    </ins-tab-item>
  </ins-tab>
</div>

{% include 'modules/website/layout/googlemaps' %}
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/axios/0.19.0/axios.min.js"></script>
{%- if context.environment == "staging" -%}
  <script src="{{ 'modules/portal/scripts/address-lookup.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  <script src="{{ 'modules/locator/scripts/locator-portal.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
{%- else -%}
  <script src="{{ 'modules/portal/scripts/address-lookup.min.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  <script src="{{ 'modules/locator/scripts/locator-portal.min.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.notice == "Success-Listing-Profile" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('success', "Locator profile has been updated.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.alert == "Error-Listing-Profile" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('error', "Error updating locator profile.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.notice == "Success-Listing-Location" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('success', "Location has been updated.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.alert == "Error-Listing-Location" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('error', "Error updating location.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.notice == "Success-Listing-Social" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('success', "Social links have been updated.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if context.flash and context.flash.alert == "Error-Listing-Social" -%}
<script>
setTimeout(() => {
  App.events.notyf('error', "Error updating social links.");
}, 200);
</script>
{%- endif -%}
